{
  // Prettier rewrites *italics* to _italics_ on save, and that breaks the
  // manuscript's cross-reference lint. An underscore is a word character, so
  // the `\b` in scripts/lint-manuscript.mjs never fires against the start of
  // _Arithmetic of Money_: a malformed chapter reference written with
  // underscores reads clean to the check built to catch it. WRITING-PLAN.md
  // sets the asterisk as the book's one italic marker for that reason, and
  // the lint rejects underscores outright.
  //
  // Prettier has no option for this; its Markdown emphasis character is not
  // configurable. So Markdown opts out of format-on-save entirely. Every
  // other language still formats normally.
  "[markdown]": {
    "editor.formatOnSave": false
  }
}
